"3D block-map reference script (storage-layout-viz saga).

The end-to-end sw-mlpl pipeline: read a columnar storage-layout.json, build
geometry with the layout library, and drive the native3d extension. Run from
the examples/viz directory so `include` and `read_text` resolve there:

  mlpl-repl -f render_native3d.mlpl           # geometry only (no native3d)
  mlpl-repl -f render_native3d.mlpl -- push   # also push to native3d

native3d is a NATIVE (wgpu/winit) extension provided by the companion
../demo-extensions repo; it is not built in sw-mlpl. Without an argument this
script only assembles + reports the geometry, so the array side is verifiable
independently. The set_boxes / set_labels / render primitives are the generic,
reusable API proposed in ../demo-extensions/docs/research.txt (not
SWTOS-specific); the demo-extensions agent implements them. The palette and
per-space offsets are visualization data, owned here in MLPL, and cover the
union of producer vocabularies (SWTOS / MLOS / MesaOS)."

include "layout.mlpl";

def u:push_to_native3d(centers, sizes, colors, ids, names) {
  "Push assembled geometry to a native3d viewer via the reusable primitives from ../demo-extensions. Requires native3d on MLPL_EXTENSION_PATH."
  n3d = load_extension("native3d")?;
  viewer = n3d:new_viewer()?;
  n3d:set_boxes(viewer, centers, sizes, colors, ids)?;
  n3d:set_labels(viewer, centers, names, ids)?;
  n3d:render(viewer)?
}

palette = {
  header: [0.55, 0.55, 0.60, 1.0],
  catalog: [0.20, 0.60, 1.00, 1.0],
  image: [1.00, 0.45, 0.20, 1.0],
  free: [0.12, 0.12, 0.14, 0.35],
  text: [0.30, 0.85, 0.40, 1.0],
  data: [0.30, 0.70, 0.85, 1.0],
  bss: [0.55, 0.45, 0.85, 1.0],
  state: [0.90, 0.85, 0.25, 1.0],
  stack: [0.90, 0.25, 0.25, 1.0],
  kernel: [0.60, 0.60, 0.65, 1.0],
};
space_offset = {
  flash: [0.0, 0.0, 0.0],
  ebr: [20.0, 0.0, 0.0],
  sysram: [40.0, 0.0, 0.0],
};

layout = parse_json(read_text("storage-layout.json")?)?;
block = at(record_get(layout, "space_block")?, 0);
geom = u:region_geometry(layout, palette, space_offset, block);
centers = record_get(geom, "centers")?;
sizes = record_get(geom, "sizes")?;
colors = record_get(geom, "colors")?;
ids = record_get(geom, "ids")?;
names = record_get(layout, "region_name")?;

print("built geometry for", tally(ids), "regions; centers", shape(centers), "colors", shape(colors));

if gt(list_len(args()), 0) {
  u:push_to_native3d(centers, sizes, colors, ids, names)
} else {
  print("native3d push skipped (pass an arg to enable, with native3d on MLPL_EXTENSION_PATH)")
}
